{
  "requirement": "Repository validation MUST continue after a failed check and report every failed\ncheck it finds in one run, each as a {term}`requirements.ci.validation_error`.\nThis is a convention for every validation error; the requirement for each check\nstates which conditions that check reports. A file that cannot be parsed, such as\na malformed `habeas.toml`, `book.toml`, or evidence file, is one failed check:\nits error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem in that file, and\nchecks that do not depend on its contents MUST still run.\n\nThe code that sequences the repository's checks carries out the first paragraph.\nA repository-validation function that collects validation errors MUST hold them\nin a parameter or local variable named `errors`, and a function with such a\nvariable is a site below; authoring code that collects errors only to abort is\nnot one. After one of its checks fails, a site MUST still run every later check\nthat does not depend on the failed check's result, including later checks in the\nsame loop iteration, and MUST NOT report one failure twice.\n\n::::{sites} error_accumulators\n```yaml\nlanguage: rust\npaths: [src, crates/habeas-sdk/src]\nexclude: [src/authoring/inputs.rs, src/authoring/tools.rs]\nrule:\n  kind: function_item\n  has:\n    stopBy: { kind: function_item }\n    any:\n      - kind: parameter\n        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }\n      - kind: let_declaration\n        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }\n  not:\n    inside:\n      stopBy: end\n      kind: mod_item\n      has: { field: name, regex: \"^tests$\" }\nmatch:\n  - \"fn check(value: &str, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"\n  - |\n    fn run() {\n        let mut errors: BTreeSet<String> = BTreeSet::new();\n        check(\"\", &mut errors);\n    }\nno_match:\n  - \"fn check(value: &str, discovery_errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"\n  - |\n    fn run() {\n        let mut problems = Vec::new();\n        check(\"\", &mut problems);\n    }\n  - |\n    mod tests {\n        fn check(errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\n    }\n```\n::::\n\n::::{violations} early_exits\n```yaml\nlanguage: rust\npaths: [src, crates/habeas-sdk/src]\nwithin: error_accumulators\nrule:\n  any:\n    - kind: try_expression\n    - kind: return_expression\n    - kind: continue_expression\n    - kind: break_expression\nmatch:\n  - |\n    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) -> Option<u8> {\n        let n = v.as_u64()?;\n        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }\n        Some(n as u8)\n    }\n  - |\n    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {\n        for item in items {\n            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); continue; }\n            if item.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }\n        }\n    }\n  - |\n    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {\n        if !v.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); return; }\n        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }\n    }\n  - |\n    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {\n        for item in items {\n            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); break; }\n        }\n        if items.is_empty() { errors.push(\"empty\".into()); }\n    }\nno_match:\n  - |\n    fn parse(v: &Value) -> Option<u8> {\n        let n = v.as_u64()?;\n        Some(n as u8)\n    }\n```\n::::",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict.** I found no adequacy gap. The tests cover the sequencing obligations, the site query matches the construct the text describes, and the snippets are adequate.\n\n**Obligations**\n1. Validation continues after a failed check and reports every failed check it finds in one run. This is carried out by the code that sequences the checks, `src/evidence.rs#fn[inspect_repository_with_progress]`.\n2. A file that cannot be parsed is one failed check. Checks that do not depend on its contents still run.\n3. No failure is reported twice.\n4. Each site of `error_accumulators` must run later independent checks after a failure, including later checks in the same loop iteration. Each site also must not report a failure twice. These obligations belong to the individual site reviews, so I did not assess them here.\n\n**Test mapping (obligations 1–3)**\n- `src/evidence.rs#mod[tests]/fn[failed_checks_do_not_hide_later_independent_checks]`:\n  - It checks that invalid or reserved names still get their text checks.\n  - It checks that every element of an input's `text` is checked, and that the definition is still resolved.\n  - It checks that a malformed hash does not hide a missing file.\n  - It checks that inline and misplaced `{fixme}` references are each reported.\n  - It asserts that no error repeats.\n- `src/evidence.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configuration_and_dependency_failures_do_not_stop_later_checks]`:\n  - A bad `habeas.toml` version, a malformed `book.toml`, an invalid evidence JSON file, and an unknown source reference are all reported in one run.\n  - Coverage setup and coverage configuration failures leave the later checks running.\n  - It checks that `habeas.toml` and `book.toml` errors each appear exactly once, and that no error is duplicated.\n- `src/evidence.rs#mod[tests]/fn[git_index_failure_is_reported_once_and_later_checks_still_run]`:\n  - A reference-discovery failure is reported exactly once.\n  - Later evidence checks still run.\n- `tests/commands.rs#fn[status_loads_nearest_workspace_file_without_validating_authoring]`:\n  - An invalid or malformed workspace file is one finding.\n  - Independent evidence findings still appear in `status` and `info`.\n- `src/evidence.rs#mod[tests]/fn[inspection_progress_preserves_validation_and_finishes_each_phase]`:\n  - An unparsable Rust source and invalid evidence JSON are both reported.\n  - Reference coverage still runs afterwards.\n- `src/evidence.rs#mod[tests]/fn[collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors]` and `...fn[schema_rejects_each_malformed_field_and_input_form]` check that multiple independent failures across and within records are all reported.\n- `src/sites.rs#mod[tests]/fn[failed_site_queries_do_not_repeat_errors_through_dependent_violations]` checks that a failing site query is reported once, and that independent queries still produce sites.\n- `src/sites.rs#mod[tests]/fn[a_violation_query_needs_a_site_query]` and `...fn[within_cannot_name_another_violation_query]` cover the site-query and violation-query placement errors for this requirement.\n- `tests/evidence_boundaries.rs#fn[an_unlistable_review_directory_is_reported_once]` and `src/index.rs#mod[tests]/fn[an_unreadable_record_is_reported_once]` check once-only reporting.\n- `src/execution_coverage/check.rs#mod[tests]/fn[accepted_exceptions_cannot_waive_invalid_measurement_and_checks_still_collect_errors]` checks that findings are not duplicated and that parse failures do not stop other findings.\n- `tests/references.rs#fn[malformed_citation_entries_do_not_hide_later_independent_errors]`, `...fn[unclosed_fences_still_report_unknown_names]` and `...fn[citation_reviews_are_required_current_and_not_orphaned]` check that malformed entries do not hide later errors.\n- `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[every_review_kind_loads_both_formats_and_reports_each_application_failure_once]` checks that each application failure is reported once and that findings contain no duplicates.\n\n**Site query (`error_accumulators`, rule 9)**\n- I ran `requirements.ci.errors/error_accumulators`.\n  - It selects the functions that carry a parameter or local named `errors`.\n  - That includes `inspect_repository_with_progress`, the validators in `src/evidence.rs` and `src/citations.rs`, and `walk` and `files` in the SDK crate's `access.rs`.\n- I searched for constructs the query might miss: destructured patterns, closure parameters, and `errors` in other positions.\n  - Only test code uses destructured `(errors, _)` patterns, and test code is outside scope.\n  - `src/refactor/tests.rs` yields no match for the rule.\n  - Non-test `errors` accumulators in `src/authoring` are only in `inputs.rs` and `tools.rs`, which the query excludes as the abort-only authoring code.\n- The one marginal selection is `src/index.rs#impl[LoadedDetailEvidence]/fn[load_path]`. It holds reported validation errors in a local `errors` and can add a `cannot read evidence` failure, so I treated it as in scope. Its test, `an_unreadable_record_is_reported_once`, cites this requirement.\n- I did not read every one of the remaining matches in full. None I saw is clearly outside scope.\n\n**Query snippets (rule 10)**\n- The site query's snippets show a parameter named `errors` and a local named `errors`. They show that `discovery_errors`, `problems`, and a function inside `mod tests` are not selected.\n- The `early_exits` violation query has one match snippet for each of `?`, `continue`, `return`, and `break`. Its no_match snippet is a function with no `errors` variable. That is adequate for a heuristic violation query.\n\nNo acknowledgments apply, and none were needed.",
